WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.831
Sun angle determines where light and shadow fall.

00:00:03.831 --> 00:00:12.501
Low sun can produce long shadows that hide features, while direct sun can create glare and wash out reflective surfaces.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:17.542
Backlighting can make an obstacle or aircraft silhouette difficult to see.

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:21.776
Lighting changes during a mission and across repeat flights.

00:00:21.776 --> 00:00:28.027
Before-and-after imagery collected at different times may show shadow differences that resemble structural change.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:33.874
Record capture time and conditions so analysts can separate illumination from scene change.

00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:38.915
Low-light conditions increase sensor noise, motion blur, and loss of detail.

00:00:38.915 --> 00:00:44.763
A camera may brighten a scene automatically while reducing sharpness or color reliability.

00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:51.416
Navigation and obstacle sensors may also have environmental limits that differ from the main camera.

00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:56.457
Night operations may have additional legal, lighting, training, and risk requirements.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:01:00.692
Operators should check current official rules and equipment guidance.

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:07.345
Darkness does not justify reliance on a video feed or automation beyond its documented capability.

00:01:07.345 --> 00:01:13.193
Plan camera orientation, exposure behavior, route direction, and observation time around the mission.

00:01:13.193 --> 00:01:18.637
Avoid sudden movements, use stable capture, and review a sample when safe.

00:01:18.637 --> 00:01:24.888
If glare or shadow blocks the required evidence, reschedule or change an authorized viewpoint.

00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:27.509
Image quality is operational quality.

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:31.743
Clear footage supports analysis, but no image removes uncertainty.

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:38.397
Document lighting limitations and do not infer detail that the sensor did not reliably capture.
